2026-05-05T09:23:49.050Z {"session_id":"ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"a9f92d5f407ec2c06","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant\\CLAUDE.md"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UCjj4ywWT4LBPbUrfD2zGU"}

2026-05-05T09:23:49.975Z {"session_id":"ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"a9f92d5f407ec2c06","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant\\CLAUDE.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant\\CLAUDE.md","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## Dev commands\n\n```bash\n# Activate venv (run once per shell session)\nvenv/Scripts/activate             # bash/Git Bash\nvenv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1         # PowerShell\n\n# Start the API server\nuvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8001\n\n# Ingest documents into Qdrant\npython ingestion/ingest.py\n```\n\n## External services\n\nBoth must be running before starting the app:\n\n```bash\ndocker compose up -d\n```\n\n| Service | Default         | Purpose                                          |\n|---------|-----------------|--------------------------------------------------|\n| Qdrant  | localhost:6333  | Vector store, collection `isel_docs`             |\n| Ollama  | localhost:11434 | LLM (`llama3.2`) and embeddings (`nomic-embed-text`) |\n\nPull required Ollama models once after first `docker compose up`:\n\n```bash\ndocker exec isel_ollama ollama pull llama3.2\ndocker exec isel_ollama ollama pull nomic-embed-text\n```\n\n## .env variables\n\n```\nOLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434\nOLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2\nOLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text\nQDRANT_HOST=localhost\nQDRANT_PORT=6333\nQDRANT_COLLECTION=isel_docs\nLLM_PROVIDER=ollama        # \"ollama\" or \"openai\"\nOPENAI_API_KEY=             # required when LLM_PROVIDER=openai\nOPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-nano  # used when LLM_PROVIDER=openai\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\nFastAPI RAG-based AI assistant for the iSEL platform. Responds in Russian (RU) and Kazakh (KZ).\n\n**Demo UI:** `http://localhost:8001/static/index.html` — glassmorphism floating widget (FAB bottom-right) built with Flaticon Uicons and Inter font. No mobile styles.\n\n**Health check:** `GET /health` returns `{\"status\": \"ok\", \"service\": \"isel-bot\"}`.\n\n### Request pipeline (`POST /api/v1/chat`)\n\nHandled in `app/routers/chat.py`. Input: `ChatRequest(message, session_id, page?, language?)`.  \nResponse: `ChatResponse(answer, source, handoff)` — `source` is `\"rule_based\"` or `\"llm\"`.\n\nThe `language` field in `ChatRequest` is accepted but **not used**. Language is auto-detected from the incoming `message` via `_detect_language()`, which checks for Kazakh-specific Cyrillic characters (ә ғ қ ң ө ұ ү і).\n\nSessions are **in-memory** (`sessions: dict[str, list[dict]] = {}` in `chat.py`) — lost on server restart.\n\n1. **Rule-based filter** (`services/rulebased.py`)  \n   Keys in `SYSTEM_COMMANDS` are matched by longest-key-first substring search (prevents short keys shadowing longer ones). Covers greetings, identity, capability, off-topic deflection, and operator handoff in both RU and KZ (`привет`, `салем`, `спасибо`, `рахмет`, etc.). Returns early without hitting RAG or the LLM.\n\n2. **Entity detection and query enrichment** (`routers/chat.py`)  \n   `_detect_entity()` scans the current message and all prior user messages for FL/UL keywords in Russian (`физ`, `юр`, `фл`, `юл`, …) and Kazakh (`жеке`, `заңды`, `занды`) terms.  \n   - If entity found AND prior history exists: pairs last user question with current message for the RAG query (assumes current message is the clarification).  \n   - If entity found but no prior history: appends entity to the RAG query.  \n   - LLM always receives `[пользователь уже указал: {entity}]` appended to the question when entity is known.  \n   Session history is capped at 10 messages; last 4 are passed to the LLM as `history_text`.\n\n3. **RAG retrieval** (`services/rag.py`)  \n   Before embedding, short domain acronyms are expanded: `ту`/`тқ` → appends \"заявление на выдачу технических условий техникалық шарттар\"; `он`/`объект`/`недвижим` → appends \"добавление объекта недвижимости\".  \n   Embeds expanded query via `nomic-embed-text` → searches top-7 chunks in Qdrant. **Embeddings always use Ollama** regardless of `LLM_PROVIDER`.  \n   Chunks whose `title` contains `Ситуация`, `Шаблон ответа`, `Жағдай`, or `Жауап үлгісі` are sorted first.  \n   Context formatted as `=== ДОКУМЕНТ: {filename} | РАЗДЕЛ: {title} ===\\n{text}`.  \n   Returns empty string (still calls LLM) when Qdrant returns nothing; router then passes `\"Контекст недоступен.\"` to the LLM.\n\n4. **LLM generation** (`services/llm_service.py`)  \n   `LLM_PROVIDER=ollama` → `_call_ollama` (POST `/api/generate`, stream=False, timeout 180 s).  \n   `LLM_PROVIDER=openai` → `_call_openai` (POST to OpenAI chat completions, timeout 30 s, max_tokens 1000).  \n   Temperature is `0.0` in both providers.  \n   System prompt uses XML tags (`<role>`, `<language_rule>`, `<history>`, `<rules>`, `<formatting>`).  \n   User prompt wraps input as `<context>`, `<question>`, `<answer>` — the open `<answer>` tag primes extraction.  \n   When `language=\"kz\"`, `<language_rule>` mandates full Kazakh translation of Russian templates and forbids any Russian in the response.  \n   `<formatting>` includes a rule to strip guillemet/quote wrapping from button names and replace with `**bold**`.\n\n### Document API (`routers/documents.py`)\n\n- `POST /api/v1/upload` — saves file with `{uuid}_{original_name}` to `data/docs/`, triggers background ingestion via `asyncio.create_task`\n- `GET /api/v1/documents` — lists files in `data/docs/`\n- `DELETE /api/v1/documents/{filename}` — removes file from disk only (does **not** remove vectors from Qdrant)\n\n### Ingestion pipeline (`ingestion/ingest.py`)\n\n`ingest()` calls `recreate_collection()` first — **every run fully wipes and recreates the Qdrant collection**. Use `ensure_collection()` directly if you need additive upserts without wiping.\n\n`split_by_situations()` uses two separate regex passes:\n1. **Meta blocks** (`Цель интента`, `Описание интента`, `Мақсаты`, `Сипаттамасы`, `Требования`, `Талаптар`) — extracted first, added at the end of the chunk list (lower RAG priority).\n2. **Situation blocks** (`Ситуация \\d+`, `Жағдай \\d+`) — each captures all content until the next situation, including any embedded `Шаблон ответа`/`Жауап үлгісі` (the template marker is stripped but its content is kept). This ensures every RAG chunk contains both the situation description and the answer template together.\n\nWhen two chunks share the same `title`, deduplication keeps the one with more text content.\n\nFalls back to fixed-size word chunking (800 words, 100-word overlap) when no situation headers are found.\n\n**Qdrant point IDs** are deterministic: `uuid.uuid5(NAMESPACE_DNS, f\"{filename}_{chunk_idx}\")`. Re-ingesting the same file updates existing points instead of creating duplicates.\n\nEach point payload includes a `\"language\"` field (`\"ru\"` or `\"kz\"`) detected by scanning chunk text for Kazakh-specific Cyrillic characters.\n\nQdrant vector size is fixed at **768** (nomic-embed-text output). `ensure_collection()` creates the collection on first run.\n\n## Key constraints\n\n- All packages under `app/` have `__init__.py` — do not delete them.\n- `frontend/` directory must exist before starting the server (`StaticFiles` mount fails otherwise).\n- `data/docs/` is the staging area for raw documents; deleting a file via the API does **not** clean up its Qdrant vectors.\n- `ingest.py` supports only `.pdf`, `.txt`, `.md` — `.docx` listed in `SUPPORTED_EXTENSIONS` in `documents.py` will be silently skipped during ingestion.\n- No test suite yet — add pytest and document commands here when added.","numLines":126,"startLine":1,"totalLines":126}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UCjj4ywWT4LBPbUrfD2zGU","duration_ms":1}

2026-05-05T09:23:50.109Z {"session_id":"ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"a9f92d5f407ec2c06","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Glob","tool_input":{"pattern":"*.toml","path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant"},"tool_response":{"filenames":[],"durationMs":711,"numFiles":0,"truncated":false},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S871xtJhC6HTKyskP8cu6p","duration_ms":712}

2026-05-05T09:26:02.833Z {"session_id":"ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"plan","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\plans\\streamed-juggling-clock.md","content":"# Plan: Replace Qdrant with LightRAG\n\n## Context\nThe platform is switching its RAG backend from Qdrant + Ollama (vector similarity) to LightRAG (knowledge graph + vectors) using GPT-4.1-nano. LightRAG extracts entities and relations from documents into a graph, enabling richer context retrieval that follows relationships between iSEL platform concepts (steps, situations, buttons, user types). The existing language handling, entity detection, rate limiting, and formatting logic in `chat.py` and `llm_service.py` are preserved.\n\n---\n\n## Key Design Decisions\n\n1. **Use `only_need_context=True`** in LightRAG `QueryParam` — LightRAG retrieves the graph context without generating a response. The existing `ask_llm()` in `llm_service.py` handles generation, language (RU/KZ), formatting, and all XML-tagged rules. This avoids duplicating LLM calls.\n\n2. **Preserve situation-level text blocks** — Rather than feeding raw full-document text to LightRAG (which would chunk across headers), use the existing `split_by_situations()` parser to produce structured text blocks and insert each block separately into LightRAG. This ensures headers like `3.1 Пользователь...` and `Ответ бота:` are entity-extraction entry points.\n\n3. **Single `LightRAG` instance** in `app/services/lightrag_service.py` — shared across routes.\n\n4. **No changes to `chat.py` entity detection or query concatenation** — the enriched query from `chat.py` flows directly to `search_docs()` which now calls LightRAG.\n\n5. **Query mode = `\"hybrid\"`** — combines graph traversal (relationships between iSEL platform steps) with vector similarity. Better than `\"naive\"` (just vectors, same as Qdrant) and cheaper than `\"mix\"`.\n\n---\n\n## Files to Create\n\n### `app/services/lightrag_service.py` (NEW)\nCentral LightRAG instance and wrappers. Contains:\n- `gpt41_nano_complete()` — async LLM func using OpenAI SDK, model `gpt-4.1-nano`, temp 0.0\n- `openai_embed()` — async embedding func using `text-embedding-3-small` (dim=1536)\n- `rag = LightRAG(working_dir=\"./data/lightrag\", llm_model_func=..., embedding_func=...)`\n- `async def initialize()` — calls `await rag.initialize_storages()` (called from lifespan)\n- `async def search_docs(query, intent, entity, language) -> str` — calls `rag.aquery(query, QueryParam(mode=\"hybrid\", only_need_context=True))`, returns context string. Prepend intent/entity to query if present.\n- `async def insert_text(text: str)` — calls `await rag.ainsert(text)`\n\n---\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n### `app/main.py`\n- Add `lifespan` async context manager\n- Call `await lightrag_service.initialize()` inside lifespan before `yield`\n- Wire lifespan to `FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)`\n\n### `app/services/rag.py` (replacement)\n- Remove all Qdrant, httpx, asyncio imports\n- Import `search_docs` from `lightrag_service` and re-export it\n- Keep the same function signature: `search_docs(query, top_k, intent, entity, page, language)` for backwards compatibility with `chat.py`\n\n### `ingestion/ingest.py` (refactor)\n- Keep: `parse_pdf()`, `parse_docx()`, `_detect_language()`, `split_by_situations()`, `split_by_chunks()`, `_extract_intent_name()`, `_slug_intent()`\n- Remove: `get_embedding()`, `ensure_collection()`, `recreate_collection()`, all Qdrant imports\n- Replace `ingest_file()`: parse doc → call `split_by_situations()` → for each chunk, format as structured text → call `lightrag_service.insert_text(chunk_text)`\n- Replace `ingest()`: scan `data/docs/` → call `ingest_file()` for each — no longer drops/recreates anything (LightRAG manages its own store)\n\nStructured chunk text format for each situation block:\n```\n[INTENT: {intent_display}]\n[SITUATION: {situation_title}]\n[LANGUAGE: {language}]\n\n{chunk_text}\n```\n\n### `app/services/llm_service.py`\n- Update `<rules>` section: mention that context comes from a knowledge graph, relations between steps are pre-extracted\n- Keep `<language_rule>`, `<formatting>`, `<intent_handling>` unchanged\n- No changes to function signature or providers\n\n### `app/routers/documents.py`\n- `_run_ingestion()` already imports `ingest_file` dynamically — no change needed since `ingest_file` signature is preserved\n\n### `docker-compose.yml`\n- Remove the `qdrant` service (no longer needed)\n- Remove the `ollama` service (LightRAG uses OpenAI embeddings, `llm_service.py` uses OpenAI LLM)\n\n### `.env` (document, don't change code for this)\n- Must have `OPENAI_API_KEY` set\n- `LLM_PROVIDER=openai` (already default)\n\n---\n\n## Files Unchanged\n- `app/routers/chat.py` — entity detection, query enrichment, session management unchanged\n- `app/services/validation.py`\n- `app/services/rate_limit.py`\n- `app/services/rulebased.py`\n- `app/utils/logger.py`\n- `app/services/task_queue.py`\n- `app/models/schemas.py`\n\n---\n\n## Install Order\n\n```bash\npip install lightrag-hku openai\n```\n\n`lightrag-hku` pulls in `networkx`, `nano-vectordb`, and `tiktoken`. The `openai` SDK is needed for the custom LLM/embedding functions.\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Install package: `pip install lightrag-hku openai`\n2. Set `OPENAI_API_KEY` in `.env`\n3. Run server: `uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8001`\n4. Check startup log for `✅ LightRAG initialized`\n5. Run ingestion: `python ingestion/ingest.py` → expect `data/lightrag/` directory to populate with `.graphml` and `.db` files\n6. Send a test chat message via the frontend and verify:\n   - Kazakh response for Kazakh input\n   - Russian response for Russian input\n   - Intent-specific answers (TU application steps, real estate object)\n7. Check `logs/` for RAG search log entries\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R5ehXiBzJ7PWvJTygG4iEK"}

